{"title":"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Extending_Line_Segments)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Extending Line Segments)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Cyclic_Quadrilaterals,_Right_Triangles,_LoC)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Cyclic Quadrilaterals, Right Triangles, LoC)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/199ae82a8817209a780c00f90a7c2eced138aa6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=120^\\circ,AB=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"184\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. If perpendiculars constructed to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/77313737edc1430265fa02356c74ce4a0dbfd957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fbfc55f2f298ffa38450e5926a1958def0bc37a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 3\\quad \\text{(B) } \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}}\\quad \\text{(C) } 5\\quad \\text{(D) } \\frac{11}{2}\\quad \\text{(E) } \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"314\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Extending_Line_Segments.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Extending_Line_Segments)\">Solution 1 (Extending Line Segments)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Extending Line Segments)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by drawing a diagram.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa08c2e7dcbccff97c2e9fba0f4079fe9dccae1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; import cse5; import geometry; size(150); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)); defaultpen(0.8); dotfactor = 4; pair A = origin; pair C = A+dir(55); pair D = A+dir(0); pair B = extension(A,A+dir(90),C,C+dir(-155)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NW); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,B--C,NW); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,A--B,W); draw(A--C--D--cycle); draw(A--B--C); draw(rightanglemark(B,C,D,2)); draw(rightanglemark(B,A,D,2)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"212\" />\nWe extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710fb5fa3adedd7a16739e543d846747adbe05b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> This gives us a couple right triangles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5309b25510f426ca00c957623bd0396c79e4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CED$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6ad40f600621d10f4435bb6f923a306af641123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEA.$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d8199b11a714357a05f6f16681656d568c310285.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; import cse5; import geometry; size(250); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)); defaultpen(0.8); dotfactor = 4; pair A = origin; pair C = A+dir(55); pair D = A+dir(0); pair B = extension(A,A+dir(90),C,C+dir(-155)); pair E = extension(A,A+2*dir(180),B,B+2*dir(-155)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NW); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,B--C,NW); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,A--B,W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SW); draw(A--C--D--cycle); draw(A--B--C); draw(rightanglemark(B,C,D,2)); draw(rightanglemark(B,A,D,2)); draw(A--E--B,dashed); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"178\" />\nWe see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd713b574a23c167aba377928abd20081cb9eb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle E = 30^\\circ$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/409f9059cc97f6eb3fee880d797e27ef4dd80fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> are 30-60-90 triangles.\n</p><p>Using the side ratios of 30-60-90 triangles, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f90dbd6ce4faf2da3c24d79f0490412d170bc17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=2BA=6$\" width=\"123\" height=\"13\" />. This tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b470de1ed8396976af276728899b97086c96391d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=BC+BE=4+6=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"240\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e882a5d7989b8169cbf98953f81f1d0634d9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA=3\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/5099336877eefda8ae2ad2708102b8c7a8f18a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC\\sim\\triangle BEA$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9491382a13324d214d9345ee434f91c5ee2b57f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{10}{3\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{CD}{3}.\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />\nSolving the equation, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9eed5c10a6b322a8b2b7b4080f19f3fd9b6600ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{CD}3&amp;=\\frac{10}{3\\sqrt{3}}\\\\ CD&amp;=3\\cdot\\frac{10}{3\\sqrt{3}}\\\\ CD&amp;=\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}}\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"114\" height=\"136\" />\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce9d021a9a972c75191214a46a5c4cd9e1712378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=\\boxed{\\textbf{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Cyclic_Quadrilaterals.2C_Right_Triangles.2C_LoC.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Cyclic_Quadrilaterals,_Right_Triangles,_LoC)\">Solution 2 (Cyclic Quadrilaterals, Right Triangles, LoC)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Cyclic Quadrilaterals, Right Triangles, LoC)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3db479e30d2dd88d5a90b0f832c2d522fc7adeca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{A}+\\angle{C} = 180^{\\circ}, ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"203\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic. Using Ptolemy's Theorem gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6e3e0a71485d2e9c4f12e8df508d426bdd306e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(1): } 4AD + 3CD = \\sqrt{37}BD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"227\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Right triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5124d12a805a9f977f2ffa46dc710c4a39ed35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABD$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea8f7a934813d1b15f985667ec7f86e7495a099.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta CBD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50f272c638d0a03844c245aa982fcc4ff181ddc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(2): } 9+AD^2=BD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901d74accc661568396ff839299c7c5c777aac3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(3):} 16+CD^2=BD^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"21\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Seeing squares in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/58473737c64d53e0635837ffc0526f79283e048e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1d3196d87757323badb2088653e72bc8a992da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(3)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, we square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75773e8f8a9093e2c1ea3efb81ae6c0295a4041a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />  and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d196fccf0a2cead75bc404ef371c2516996914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(4): } 16AD^2+9CD^2 + 24AD\\cdot CD = 37BD^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"356\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We don't like that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f80c65b2b47751a9f0a384f0dfb1822d7b85c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD\\cdot CD$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> term, but fortunately LoC exists: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341f914ffc64e4172f40632ddbd103d1b96c693a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37 = AD^2 + CD^2 - 2*AD*CD*\\cos(60^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"347\" height=\"21\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f80c65b2b47751a9f0a384f0dfb1822d7b85c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD\\cdot CD$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> and plugging it into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da354d4e7882d3812db8ca5fc9b2f1571d65c66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(4)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, and using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f0d16cefc9a3524d1b5e080200f88c18e3945d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD^2 = 7 + CD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66ccbdeaa3fba98c92ec6e1fa9230278637c550e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD^2 = 16 + CD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> from the first two equations, gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fc91d322be13390fb4e3a9588e22235d495294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40(CD^2+7)+33CD^2 - 24\\cdot 37 = 37(16+CD^2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"392\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def34299c7bc9d3594c3d644c49109c43e47173c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = \\boxed{\\textbf{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"80\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~PureSwag\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME\" title=\"1992 AHSME\">1992 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183033\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 296/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9283/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.214      1 -total\n 57.79%    7.058      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 39.71%    4.850      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12951:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183033 and revision id 179436. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}